  "empirical_findings": {
    "freshness_first_improvement": "Domain-specific bullion directional rules (mapping hawkish Fed and strong dollar to bearish, and dovish pauses, safe-haven geopolitics, and central bank buying to bullish) improve directional accuracy of news features from 33.3% (generic FinBERT sentiment) to 38.1% (fresh bullion impact). However, market-only features continue to demonstrate superior directional accuracy (52.4%) and lower RMSE (\u20b977.97/g vs \u20b980.52/g).",
    "deployment_discipline": "In accordance with rigorous quantitative trading principles, the live news intelligence signal is decoupled from mechanical price forecasting. Live news intelligence is surfaced as an independent, freshness-ranked macro consensus with driver attribution, rather than forcing noisy text embeddings into the low-sample quantitative price regression model."
  },
  "conclusion": "Freshness-prioritized bullion news features show improved alignment with market drivers compared to generic sentiment. However, market-derived financial features remain the primary predictive driver for next-day Indian bullion rates. Live news intelligence should be treated as an independent macro consensus and risk indicator.",
